      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please do not adjust your insulin without consulting your healthcare provider first, as this is a complex medical decision. For an acute low blood sugar episode, the priority is raising your immediate sugar levels with simple carbs like juice. Insulin can worsen hypoglycemia, so it is best to treat the low first and then monitor your levels before making any dosing changes. If you are highly concerned about future spikes, check your blood glucose now, and if you are stable, you can follow your established mealtime plan.",
